          "eventMappings": [
<% all_in = "globalVars.assets_decided === true && globalVars.irina_fate_decided === true && globalVars.flag1_submitted === true && globalVars.flag2_submitted === true && globalVars.flag3_submitted === true && globalVars.flag4_submitted === true && globalVars.debrief_played !== true && globalVars.start_debrief_cutscene !== true" %>
<%# PASS 2 review B2 / minor 13. The final state change can land inside a phone
    chat (Satoshi-KO decision, Irina-KO relay) or the drop-site UI (last flag).
    Opening the debrief then would tear that UI down mid-line, so those cases
    wait for the UI to close: every minigame close emits minigame_completed
    (#exit_conversation, flag success) or minigame_failed (the X / Esc),
    base-minigame.js:94-104. The two person-chats close with conversation_closed.
    room_entered on every room is the backstop if the player walks away.
    start_debrief_cutscene is the synchronous latch: a person-chat close emits
    both conversation_closed and minigame_completed, and setGlobal runs before
    the next listener evaluates (npc-manager.js:541-553), so only one opens.
